    "title": "Liberty cancels board meeting ahead of state deadline - NewsBreak",
    "text": "8 days ago\nLiberty Elementary School District canceled the board meeting scheduled for Monday, Oct. 1 as the board did not meet quorum. Michael Todd, board president posted an announcement on his Facebook page stating he was sick, two board members were on vacation and another was delayed at their job.\nLiberty staff was set to approve the Annual Financial Report , which is required to be approved and submitted to the Arizona Department of Education before Wednesday, Oct. 15.\nVisit liberty25.org for more information on rescheduling.",
